{
  "title": "Order processing: services and data flow",
  "description": "How an order moves through the order processing services; no infrastructure is shown. A customer uses the web app, which calls the Order service through the API gateway. The Order service checks stock with the Inventory service (backed by a Redis stock cache), charges through the Billing service and its payment provider, and stores the order in the Orders database. It then publishes an OrderPlaced event to a Kafka topic; the Notification worker consumes it and sends e-mail through an outside e-mail API. Solid lines are synchronous calls, dashed lines are asynchronous events.",
